title: WidgetExamples

! `<$mermaid>` Widget Examples

!! 1. Direct Attribute Usage

```html
<$mermaid text="flowchart LR; A[Left] --> B[Center] --> C[Right];"/>
```

<$mermaid text="flowchart LR; A[Left] --> B[Center] --> C[Right];"/>

!! 2. Inline Widget Body

```html
<$mermaid>
flowchart TD
    Alpha[Alpha Node] --> Beta[Beta Node]
    Beta --> Gamma[Gamma Node]
</$mermaid>
```

<$mermaid>
flowchart TD
    Alpha[Alpha Node] --> Beta[Beta Node]
    Beta --> Gamma[Gamma Node]
</$mermaid>

!! 3. Alignment

!!! Left Aligned

```html
<$mermaid align="left" text="graph LR; A-->B;"/>
```

<$mermaid align="left" text="graph LR; A-->B;"/>

!!! Right Aligned

```html
<$mermaid align="right" text="graph LR; X-->Y;"/>
```

<$mermaid align="right" text="graph LR; X-->Y;"/>

!! 4. Explicit Theme Override

!!! Forest Theme (`theme="forest"`)

```html
<$mermaid theme="forest" text="pie title Languages Used
    'JavaScript' : 55
    'WikiText' : 30
    'CSS' : 15
"/>
```

<$mermaid theme="forest" text="pie title Languages Used
    'JavaScript' : 55
    'WikiText' : 30
    'CSS' : 15
"/>

!!! Neutral Theme (`theme="neutral"`)

```html
<$mermaid theme="neutral" text="graph TD; A[Clean Design] --> B[Neutral Tones];"/>
```

<$mermaid theme="neutral" text="graph TD; A[Clean Design] --> B[Neutral Tones];"/>

!! 5. Error Handling & Diagnostics

The plugin catches malformed diagram syntax and renders an accessible error alert box inline without crashing the wiki.

